  "notes": "Cash basis. Aligned with FY2024 (2026-11-12): the Sewer fund column of the governmental funds statements is recorded as business-type (cash measure, 671,524 -> 964,314, p5); governmental totals and fund balances are the Total Governmental column minus the Sewer column; Licenses, fees, and permits split by fund column; Sewer cash in bank and restricted net position tagged business-type; Sewer statement-column detail removed. Statement lines from the Total Governmental column (p6). Balances are printed as fund balance (cash basis), so beginning/ending_fund_balance are filled and cash fields left null; ending cash in bank 4,548,806, cash with county treasurer 18,682 and certificates of deposit 200,636 are on the balance sheet. Transfers in (out) total column is nil (Keno 259,760 out to General/Parks in), so transfers_in/out null. Bond anticipation note proceeds 600,000 = debt_proceeds. Balance sheet from the Statement of Fund Balances - Governmental Funds Total column (equals the government-wide Statement of Net Position, p1). Detail: General Fund from the combining schedule by department (p8-9, one line per department column); Keno, TIF, Debt Service and Capital Projects statement-column detail removed to match FY2024 (2026-11-12). The all-funds budget schedule (p7) is not recorded, to avoid double counting. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
